## References

- J. Barzilai and J. M. Borwein (1988), Two-point step size gradient methods, IMA Journal of Numerical Analysis, 8(1), 141–148. https://doi.org/10.1093/imanum/8.1.141
- Y. H. Dai and Y. Yuan (1999), A nonlinear conjugate gradient method with a strong global convergence property, SIAM Journal on Optimization, 10(1), 177–182. https://doi.org/10.1137/S1052623497318992
- R. Fletcher and C. M. Reeves (1964), Function minimization by conjugate gradients, The Computer Journal, 7(2), 149–154. https://doi.org/10.1093/comjnl/7.2.149
- W. W. Hager and H. Zhang (2005), A new conjugate gradient method with guaranteed descent and an efficient line search, SIAM Journal on Optimization, 16(1), 170–192. https://doi.org/10.1137/030601880
- M. R. Hestenes and E. Stiefel (1952), Methods of conjugate gradients for solving linear systems, Journal of Research of the National Bureau of Standards, 49(6), 409–436. https://doi.org/10.6028/jres.049.044
- D. P. Kingma and J. Ba (2015), Adam: A method for stochastic optimization, 3rd International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR 2015), arXiv:1412.6980. https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.1412.6980
